    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "How can I map something to a default keybind overridden by mini?\r\n\r\nIn my case, I want to use `gx`, but on a different key. Mini operators uses `gx` as the prefix for exchange, and remapping just that key messes up my muscle memory (many mini keymaps use g<something> as a prefix).",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">How can I map something to a default keybind overridden by mini?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In my case, I want to use <code class=\"notranslate\">gx</code>, but on a different key. Mini operators uses <code class=\"notranslate\">gx</code> as the prefix for exchange, and remapping just that key messes up my muscle memory (many mini keymaps use g as a prefix).</p>",
    "bodyText": "How can I map something to a default keybind overridden by mini?\nIn my case, I want to use gx, but on a different key. Mini operators uses gx as the prefix for exchange, and remapping just that key messes up my muscle memory (many mini keymaps use g as a prefix).",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2024-07-03T17:58:16Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Unfortunately, there is no easy answer to that.\r\n\r\nThe most robust way is to use some version of the following code (here it is for your use case):\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal remap = function(mode, lhs_from, lhs_to)\r\n  local keymap = vim.fn.maparg(lhs_from, mode, false, true)\r\n  local rhs = keymap.callback or keymap.rhs\r\n  if rhs == nil then error('Could not remap from ' .. lhs_from .. ' to ' .. lhs_to) end\r\n  vim.keymap.set(mode, lhs_to, rhs, { desc = keymap.desc })\r\nend\r\nremap('n', 'gx', '<Leader>gx')\r\nremap('x', 'gx', '<Leader>gx')\r\n```",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Unfortunately, there is no easy answer to that.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The most robust way is to use some version of the following code (here it is for your use case):</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local remap = function(mode, lhs_from, lhs_to)\n  local keymap = vim.fn.maparg(lhs_from, mode, false, true)\n  local rhs = keymap.callback or keymap.rhs\n  if rhs == nil then error('Could not remap from ' .. lhs_from .. ' to ' .. lhs_to) end\n  vim.keymap.set(mode, lhs_to, rhs, { desc = keymap.desc })\nend\nremap('n', 'gx', '&lt;Leader&gt;gx')\nremap('x', 'gx', '&lt;Leader&gt;gx')\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">remap</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">mode</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">lhs_from</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">lhs_to</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">keymap</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">fn</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">maparg</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">lhs_from</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">mode</span>, <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span>, <span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">rhs</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">rhs</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">rhs</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">nil</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">then</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">error</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>Could not remap from <span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">..</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">lhs_from</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">..</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span> to <span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">..</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">lhs_to</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">set</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">mode</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">lhs_to</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">rhs</span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">desc</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">desc</span> })\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">remap</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>gx<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;Leader&gt;gx<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">remap</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>x<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>gx<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;Leader&gt;gx<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)</pre></div>",
            "bodyText": "Unfortunately, there is no easy answer to that.\nThe most robust way is to use some version of the following code (here it is for your use case):\nlocal remap = function(mode, lhs_from, lhs_to)\n  local keymap = vim.fn.maparg(lhs_from, mode, false, true)\n  local rhs = keymap.callback or keymap.rhs\n  if rhs == nil then error('Could not remap from ' .. lhs_from .. ' to ' .. lhs_to) end\n  vim.keymap.set(mode, lhs_to, rhs, { desc = keymap.desc })\nend\nremap('n', 'gx', '<Leader>gx')\nremap('x', 'gx', '<Leader>gx')",
